meta {
  name: Space List Repo Ops
  type: http
  seq: 155
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/xrpc/com.atproto.space.listRepoOps?space=at://did:plc:authorityaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa/space/org.example.bucket/main&repo={{did}}&limit=100
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

params:query {
  space: at://did:plc:authorityaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa/space/org.example.bucket/main
  repo: {{did}}
  limit: 100
  ~since:
  ~cursor:
  ~excludeValues: false
}

docs {
  Page a permissioned repo's oplog — the primary incremental sync mechanism. Each entry is
  {rev, collection, rkey, cid, prev}: cid null = delete, prev null = create, ops sharing a rev
  belong to one atomic batch. The record's current value is inlined for creates/updates unless
  "excludeValues=true" or a later op superseded it.

  "since" returns ops strictly after that rev; the cursor continues a paginated response. A
  response reaching the head of the oplog includes the current signed commit and no cursor —
  the syncer compares the commit hash against its own running LtHash fold. The oplog is a
  transport optimization with no history guarantee (compacted after a retention window, reset
  on migration); a mismatched fold means heal via getRepo.
}
